    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d592-a2">

                <pb facs="0698" n="602" xml:id="pg602"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Altoona</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-06-29"><hi rendition="#italic">June 29,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#italic">To whom it may concern:</hi></p>
                <p>This is to certify that I was present when the following children of Mr. M. W.
                    Pipping and wife were born, viz: Anio Pipping was born March 13, 1884; Alf
                    Pipping was born November 24, 1885; Ingevald Pipping was born December 28,
                    1887.</p>
                <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jno. Fay, M. D.</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">State of Pennsylvania</hi>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">County of Blair, ss:</hi></p>
                <p>Personally before me, a notary public in and for said county and State, came John
                    Fay, M. D., who, being duly sworn according to law, deposeth and saith that the
                    statement made above is true and correct</p>
                <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jno. Fay, M. D.</hi></p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">Sworn to and subscribed before me <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1895-06-29">the 29th day of June, A. D.
                            1895</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. Hamor</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Notary Public.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
